diff -ruN a/thirdjam/Public/JamCartridge.h b/thirdjam/Public/JamCartridge.h
--- a/thirdjam/Public/JamCartridge.h
+++ b/thirdjam/Public/JamCartridge.h
@@ -682,6 +682,17 @@
 	// another body's touch and through his own bounce off a body: it leaves him by a shot, a pass, a poke, a lift, a check that stumbles or fells him.
 	// false = thirdjam.
 	bool bCarryHoldsBody = false;
+	// THIRDLIFE PATCH 0004 (experiment E05, pillars 2 and 5; the owner's R-0041 "skater with puck will need slight speed reduction ... to incentivize
+	// passing" and R-0045 "sprint speed of defenders should be always higher"). Nobody glides faster than he can skate: a skater moving faster along his
+	// facing than his own top speed at a full stick in his present state (carrying or free, sprinting or not, the breakaway burst while it runs) loses
+	// this many m/s every second until he is at that top. thirdjam takes speed above the top only by the glide's 0.147 m/s2, so a sprint's 14.55 m/s
+	// outlives its bar by many seconds (PLAY.md section 4 item 12) and a skater who takes the puck at 12.65 m/s carries it at 12.65, not at the carrier's
+	// 10.12. Easing the stick still glides as before (the test is against the FULL stick's top), and a lunge is left alone. 0 = thirdjam.
+	double OverTopDecelMps2 = 0.0;
+	// ... and the bar is the sprint's cost. In thirdjam a held sprint key with an empty bar sprints again on the first frame the bar holds one tick (every
+	// other frame: the gym's carrier sprints 290 of 401 frames on a 180-frame bar), so the bar never ends a held sprint. With this share above 0 a sprint
+	// that is not already running STARTS only with at least this share of the full bar; one that runs goes on to the last tick as before. 0 = thirdjam.
+	double SprintRestartShare = 0.0;
 };
